"Notable Nativities" was written to demonstrate the validity of new
reliable methods for the rectification of natal charts. This is of prime
importance, as a reliable interpretation is only possible from a correctly
rectified chart.


   It Is my experience that the individuality of any natal chart hinges on
the exact Identification of Its angles, not on interplanetary aspects which
will be very much the same for all persons born on the same day. Indeed
for the slower planets some aspects may continue for weeks, even months.
These characteristics also depend on the position of the Ascendant in a
sign of the tropical Zodiac, interplanetary aspects that have no connection   ,
to angles or house cusps    only become active when and if these aspects
mature by progressed or regressed directions in the Secondary directio­
nal system.


