    As a schoolboy, Nelson Page came to Buenos Aires when his parents
emigrated to the Argentine, After a commercial education, he went into
business at the age of 18. At this time, he became interested in astrology.
With all of the seriousness that we can expect from a man with such a
scientific mind, he improved his knowledge in mathematics and achieved a
solid command of astrology.
These extensive studies, with the emphasis on mathematics and statis­
tics, greatly helped his outstanding career, in later years, up to his death,
he held a highly responsible position in an insurance company. He married
at 25 and had three children. His eldest son, himself a serious astrologer,
attained a degree as a nuclear physicist.
   Nelson Page's   salient importance lies in the fact that he recognized,
and subsequently publicized, the actual basis of serious astrological
research--the scientifically provable rectification.
 Together with his friend Vendel Polich ( his collaborator for over twenty
years) he solved many of the trigonometrical problems of astrology and
discovered the Topocentric House System retrospectively,that          is via
events on narrowly-timed births.
