The most effective combination in this chart is the triple conjunction of
MOON, MC, REGULUS and the conjunction of SATURN to the Ascendant.
Experience shows that people who become famous or Infamous and who
have decisively influenced the development of history have prominent
fixed stars in important places of the horoscope, i.e. on Angles, House
Cusps or in conjunctions with planets. In many unimpressive-looking ho­
roscopes of V.P's with no angular planets, we find prominent fixed stars
on MC or ASC. REGULUS       is the fixed star of kings and leaders of state, it
has a neutral character. Here on MC it promises fame and, with the MOON,
popularity. The trine of PLUTO and the sextile of JUPITER strengthen and
improve the positive characteristics of rising SATURN, which in many ho­
roscopes, under bad cosmic conditions, appears as a pure malefic. In our
case Saturn gave perseverance, steadfastness and also persistence. Under
these conditions Saturn should also promise satisfactory health and a
comparatively long life. The astonishingly accurate JUPITER-PLUTO oppo­
sition does not make any impression at the moment, because this is a
non-individual aspect, lasting for days or even weeks. However their close
connection to the'ASC (sextile and trine) and near the III - IX axis,
brought great success in internal (111) and external (IX) politics. This
combination is of course also favourable for propaganda and elections (III).
VENUS and MARS, although in insignificant positions, are in a wide sextile
and, at least, they     helped   Margaret Thatcher not to lose the audacious
war enterprise in Argentina.
